From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:26:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_ecm: Resend a notification that failed to
 queue on resume
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ecm_do_notify() advances notify_state before it queues the request. If
usb_ep_queue() fails, for example with -EAGAIN while the UDC is
suspended, the CONNECT or SPEED_CHANGE notification is dropped for
good. The host then never learns the link state: macOS keeps the
interface without carrier although the gadget's own netdev carrier is
up, until the gadget is rebound.

Restore notify_state when queueing fails, and try the pending
notification again from ecm_resume(). Clear it when the function is
disabled, so a notification is not sent for an old configuration.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 7dcb77b9 and omarchy-ipad5
 patches/periph/usb-resume/0002 (J71t ledger 7.2); resume resends only
 the pending notification (ecm_do_notify()) instead of restarting the
 CONNECT/SPEED sequence, and ecm_disable() clears the pending state]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ecm.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ecm.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ecm.c
index e495bac4e..dfbc23cb1 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ecm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ecm.c
@@ -371,6 +371,7 @@ static void ecm_do_notify(struct f_ecm *ecm)
 	struct usb_cdc_notification	*event;
 	struct usb_composite_dev	*cdev = ecm->port.func.config->cdev;
 	__le32				*data;
+	u8				state = ecm->notify_state;
 	int				status;
 
 	/* notification already in flight? */
@@ -417,6 +418,11 @@ static void ecm_do_notify(struct f_ecm *ecm)
 	status = usb_ep_queue(ecm->notify, req, GFP_ATOMIC);
 	if (status < 0) {
 		atomic_dec(&ecm->notify_count);
+		/*
+		 * Keep the notification pending: a suspended UDC rejects the
+		 * request (e.g. with -EAGAIN), and ecm_resume() sends it then.
+		 */
+		ecm->notify_state = state;
 		DBG(cdev, "notify --> %d\n", status);
 	}
 }
@@ -625,6 +631,7 @@ static void ecm_disable(struct usb_function *f)
 
 	usb_ep_disable(ecm->notify);
 	ecm->notify->desc = NULL;
+	ecm->notify_state = ECM_NOTIFY_NONE;
 }
 
 /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
@@ -886,6 +893,9 @@ static void ecm_resume(struct usb_function *f)
 	DBG(cdev, "ECM Resume\n");
 
 	gether_resume(&ecm->port);
+
+	/* Send a notification that could not be queued while suspended */
+	ecm_do_notify(ecm);
 }
 
 static int ecm_get_status(struct usb_function *f)
